1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,222
Meet MerchantLens, a problem intake interviewer built for the Paytm and AI Garage buildathon.

2
00:00:06,222 --> 00:00:10,222
It turns ambiguous merchant conversations into evidence-linked problem briefs.

3
00:00:10,222 --> 00:00:16,000
This is the deployed Cloud Run app, using clearly labelled synthetic merchant data.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,632
We begin with consent, a merchant alias, and the interview language.

5
00:00:20,632 --> 00:00:24,000
Public demo drafts stay in the visitor's browser.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,526
This recording uses typed synthetic responses.

7
00:00:26,526 --> 00:00:32,000
Browser voice controls are available, and the merchant reviews the text before sending.

8
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:39,837
The merchant says the Soundbox was silent and thinks two thousand four hundred rupees were lost.

9
00:00:39,837 --> 00:00:45,224
The guided interviewer does not accept that as verified financial loss.

10
00:00:45,224 --> 00:00:48,653
It asks what the amount actually represents.

11
00:00:48,653 --> 00:00:56,000
This is a labelled rules-based turn, with a concrete clarification instead of a generic questionnaire.

12
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:02,118
We clarify that the amount was affected payment value, not a confirmed loss.

13
00:01:02,118 --> 00:01:09,176
Now we explicitly select live Gemini and report that the merchant app showed successful payments.

14
00:01:09,176 --> 00:01:14,353
The next question separates bank settlement from the missing audio announcement.

15
00:01:14,353 --> 00:01:20,000
The application preserves the distinction between a merchant report and independent verification.

16
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:31,265
The agent control room exposes the actual run: extraction, provenance verification, parallel critique and context retrieval, question planning, and a code policy gate.

17
00:01:31,265 --> 00:01:36,653
Model calls, tokens, tools, and timing come from the completed request.

18
00:01:36,653 --> 00:01:39,592
Source removal shows dependencies, not causation.

19
00:01:39,592 --> 00:01:44,000
Retrieved product context is kept separate from merchant evidence.

20
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:48,840
We finish the remaining questions with the labelled synthetic sample answers.

21
00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:56,760
The merchant describes unknown settlement, recurrence, checkout disruption, the phone-sharing workaround, earlier troubleshooting, constraints, and a useful outcome.

22
00:01:56,760 --> 00:01:58,960
Questions adapt to captured information.

23
00:01:58,960 --> 00:02:06,000
Full topic coverage means the topics were addressed; it does not make the claims independently true.

24
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:11,000
In the evidence chain, each observation links to its original merchant quote.

25
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:13,917
Selecting the quote highlights the source turn.

26
00:02:13,917 --> 00:02:20,167
The amount interpretation is clarified, while financial loss, settlement verification, and root cause remain open.

27
00:02:20,167 --> 00:02:26,000
A builder gets both the reported problem and the gaps that still need investigation.

28
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,872
The synthetic interview includes a customer name.

29
00:02:28,872 --> 00:02:32,564
Removing it scrubs retained transcript text, observations, and history.

30
00:02:32,564 --> 00:02:37,487
A correction or redaction creates a new version and invalidates previous approvals.

31
00:02:37,487 --> 00:02:42,000
The merchant controls what is retained and what can be exported.

32
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,500
The internal brief preserves investigation detail.

33
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:49,500
The anonymized version omits names, exact amounts, source identifiers, and raw quotes.

34
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:53,667
Each audience requires a separate approval for the current version.

35
00:02:53,667 --> 00:02:57,417
The agent cannot approve itself or submit anything externally.

36
00:02:57,417 --> 00:03:02,000
The merchant reviews the draft and explicitly approves the selected audience.

37
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:08,462
Approval unlocks actual JSON and Markdown downloads, ready for a builder or operations reviewer.

38
00:03:08,462 --> 00:03:14,000
Public demo interviews stay in each browser; private cloud checkpoints remain protected.

39
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:23,290
Seven guided probes test money ambiguity, unavailable bank evidence, early stopping, prompt injection, device damage and fabricated sources.

40
00:03:23,290 --> 00:03:30,000
These observable regression checks do not establish live-model accuracy or production interview quality.

41
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:34,500
MerchantLens turns conversations into traceable briefs with human review.

42
00:03:34,500 --> 00:03:37,000
Live Gemini and exports work.

43
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:39,500
Paytm APIs are not connected.

44
00:03:39,500 --> 00:03:44,000
Voice transcription accuracy still requires a human spoken-input test.
